[1.029,"o","\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m  [12]  INFERENCE — Live LLM on GCO\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n\r\n"]
[0.0,"o","  \u001b[2mGCO isn't just for batch jobs — it also manages multi-region\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[2minference endpoints. We deployed a vLLM endpoint at the start\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[2mof this demo so the GPU could provision while we covered other\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[2mfeatures. Let's see if it's ready.\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[33m\u001b[1m▸ Checking if the inference endpoint is ready\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n"]
[0.0,"o","  \u001b[2mThe endpoint was deployed with a single command at the start.\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[2mEKS Auto Mode provisioned a GPU node, pulled the vLLM image,\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n"]
[0.0,"o","  \u001b[2mand loaded the facebook/opt-125m model — all automatically.\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n"]
[1.222,"o","  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m✓ Inference pod is Kubernetes-ready.\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n"]
[0.0,"o","  \u001b[2mKubernetes readiness is local; validating one real generation through the global route.\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n"]
[4.987,"o","  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m✓ End-to-end global inference route is ready.\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n\r\n"]
[0.0,"o","  \u001b[33m\u001b[1m▸ Sending a prompt to the endpoint\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n"]
[0.0,"o","  \u001b[2mThe shared inference route is already registered on the internal ALB.\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n"]
[0.0,"o","  \u001b[2mRequests traverse API Gateway → Global Accelerator → ALB → authenticated proxy → vLLM.\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[2mAPI Gateway validates SigV4; the private backend hop uses private-root TLS plus a request-bound HMAC.\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[35m$ \u001b[37m\u001b[1mgco inference invoke demo-llm -p 'The benefits of GPU orchestration for ML workloads are: 1)' --max-tokens 80\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[2m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n"]
[2.378,"o","  i POST /inference/demo-llm/v1/completions\r\n  \r\n  Distribution ofocating resources: Like other computational tasks, distributed class operations-based applications are handled by software. Performance and flexibility for the new AHIT and cluster scheduler technology allows optimizing workloads. 2) Multiple virtual machine number and scheduling cycles on GPUs. 3) Multiple clustering algorithms for data analysis, larger throughput and more connections. 4) Increase workloads for the application stack and network.\r\n  \r\n"]
[0.132,"o","  \u001b[2m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n"]
[2.025,"o","  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m✓ Live LLM response from a GPU that didn't exist minutes ago.\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n"]
